The Association of Powell Place Home Owners, served by Certified Mail on July 23, 2015;
Plaintiff further moves this Court pursuant to Rule 21 of the Ohio Rules of Civil Procedure for an order dismissing John Doe, Name Unknown, the Unknown Spouse of Alanda Ross (if any) and Jane Doe, Name Unknown, the Unknown Spouse of John B. Harris, AKA John Harris (if any) from this action. Plaintiff has learned that the foregoing defendants do not have an interest in the property that is the subject of this foreclosure action.
Plaintiff acknowledges that the County Treasurer may claim an interest in the Property as a result of taxes, assessments and penalties that may be due on the Property. Plaintiff further acknowledges that, under Ohio law, liens securing the payment of taxes, assessments and penalties on property are first in terms of priority. As a result, the Treasurer will be given senior priority to Plaintiff's claim.
Plaintiff acknowledges that all personal obligations of Alanda Ross on the promissory note that is the subject of this foreclosure action have been discharged under the United States Bankruptcy Code. As a result, Plaintiff does not seek personal judgment against said defendant but rather seeks only a finding of default on the note and an order and decree of foreclosure.
